module Core

### Represents the protocol for values that can be lowered to a `SerialValue` tree.
### `Serializable` is auto-derived for every user aggregate (records, entities, …): the compiler
### synthesizes `serialize()` by walking every member variable, exactly like `$represent`. Because
### the body is always generated, aggregate category protocols (`RecordType`, `EntityType`, …) may
### `obey Serializable` safely — unlike `Equatable`/`Hashable`, which are hand-written promises and
### would leave an abstract method behind. A type may hand-override `serialize()` to hide a field or
### customize its encoding; format encoders (JSON, MessagePack, …) run over the resulting tree.
protocol Serializable
  ### Lowers this value to a `SerialValue` tree. Total — never fails.
  ### :returns: The serialized representation of this value.
  @readonly
  routine Me.serialize() -> SerialValue
